y for the archaeol foundation  they just obviously don't like this  journalistic integrity their question  do you think they were right to do the  interview is it something that you would  have recommended to them to do  i think so i think obviously there's  been so much here saying so much you  know  the media vilifying megan it was an  opportunity for her  to say how it is you know these are the  facts you know before it was all white  noise and second guessing what  was going on but now we've actually  heard it from as i say the horse's mouth  you know here we go um and do you think  you know we understand that they've said  that this this is going to be their last  word on the subject i mean  do you think it will be do you think it  should be  i think i think it will be and i think  it should be i think they've drawn a  line in sand they've had an opportunity  to  you know voice their side and now it's  time for them to move on  what advice would you give him in terms  of moving on and  and how he should be living his life now  um obviously i think with obviously  megan being six months pregnant you know  his priority now is  is his family um he talks at the end  about how he wants to  heal those relationships between his  brother and his father so  i'd like to see see that happen and i'd  like to see both families in both sides  of water and  getting on i mean how about how bad is  all those relationships do you think and  and is it possible  for them to be healed of course you know  any family there's always there always  tend to be arguments i do think you know  anything any sort of relationship can be  healed you know it's going to take time  it's going to take patience obviously  that he now has to  his priorities are megan archie and the  the up and coming baby um but hopefully  there'll be times an opportunity for him  to  to come back and sort of you know  rebuild those relationships  uh dean stott a friend of prince harry  uh great to talk to you today 